The desk merged every report with a matching subject line into #4471 and marked it known: one
parser bug, one fix queued. The desk's own code disagrees. `causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`
places a report by its tenant's locale and booking form, and it finds two causes in the ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one problem. Two. The queued parser fix leaves the second one open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 really holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is built from `reports-4471.json` at render time. The export has 427 rows; 15 are the
same report twice, so 412 reports, as the desk counted. The intake tag is a guess from the
reporter's browser and is wrong for 38 of them.

## Problem 1 · the shared parser reads dates month first

The parser in sched-prod reads every date month first. Eleven tenants write the day first, so
7 April goes out as 4 July. This is what the incident page describes, and the queued fix is for it.
Ticket: [problem 1 of 2](https://github.com/fchrapek/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

Five of its reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). They stay counted by
tenant, as the table footnotes them.

## Problem 2 · booking-v3 prints the wrong date hint

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Three day-first tenants run it
(alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour). Their people type what the hint says, and the form
reads it the tenant's way. Every one of these reports came through the form. The parser fix does
not touch this; the form has to print the tenant's own order.
Ticket: [problem 2 of 2](https://github.com/fchrapek/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Why the desk missed it

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Two reports can
share a subject and have different causes; the dedupe page's explorer already shows the pairs.
Merging on cause needs the tenant file, which intake never looks up.

## Outcome

The desk closed #4471 on 5 October. Problem 1 is fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
Problem 2 will not be fixed: the booking-v3 form was retired, and the hint went with it. Both
tickets above are closed with those reasons.

## What to do next time

- When the next big ticket comes in, run `CauseTable` on it before marking it known.
- Merge on cause, not on subject: that needs the tenant file, which intake never looks up.

